pytest.ini  - Just learn the definition.
----------
pytest.ini is created to configure pytest in one central place so you don’t have to repeat settings
or options in every command or test file.

***Purpose of pytest.ini
It is used to store global pytest configurations, such as:

✔** 1. Define markers
So pytest stops showing warnings like "PytestUnknownMarkWarning".

    EX: ---mention inside pytest.ini file-----
    [pytest]
    markers =
        smoke: smoke test cases
        regression: regression test cases

✔** 2. Set test discovery rules
You can define:
    Which files are considered tests
    Name patterns
    Folder patterns

    EX: ---mention inside pytest.ini file-----
        python_files = test_*.py
        python_classes = Test*
        python_functions = test_*

✔** 3. Add default command-line options
To avoid typing them every time.

    Ex: ---mention inside pytest.ini file-----
    addopts = -v -s --maxfail=1

✔** 4. Configure logging

    EX:---mention inside pytest.ini file-----
        log_cli = true
        log_level = INFO

✔** 5. Set test paths
So pytest only runs tests from specific directories.

    EX:---mention inside pytest.ini file-----
        testpaths =
            tests
            api_tests

